    {
      "id": "2263dbcf-062a-514d-825a-27f78cf3996a",
      "name": "Sticky Note t1/desc",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -600,
        40
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 520,
        "height": 1180,
        "content": "## Archive Instagram Stories to Google Sheets\n\nInstagram Stories disappear after 24 hours, so if you did not look, it never happened. This workflow checks the profiles you care about three times a day and writes every new story to a Google Sheet before it expires: who posted it, when, whether it was an ad, the caption, the place tag, and a direct link to the image or video file.\n\n**Who's it for**\nSocial media managers building a competitor swipe file, brand teams keeping a record of what partners and creators posted about them, and agencies who need evidence of what a client's rivals were running last month.\n\n**How it works**\n1. A schedule trigger fires every 8 hours, so nothing expires unseen\n2. The Apify node runs the Instagram Stories Scraper for your list of public profiles\n3. A filter drops diagnostic rows, keeping only real stories\n4. Remove Duplicates remembers every story ID it has already saved, so re-checking the same profile never creates a duplicate row\n5. The fields you care about are appended to your Google Sheet\n\n**Setup**\n1. Create a free Apify account and paste your API token into the Apify credential\n2. Connect your Google account in the Sheets node and pick a spreadsheet and tab\n3. Replace the example profiles with the public accounts you want to archive, then run once to test\n\n**Good to know**\nOnly public profiles are readable, and only stories that are live at the moment of the run. Every 8 hours is the sweet spot: often enough that a 24-hour story cannot slip past, cheap enough to leave on. Collection costs about $0.0004 per story, so watching three busy accounts around the clock is usually a few cents a month. There is no login and no cookie to supply.\n\nActor: https://apify.com/dami_studio/instagram-stories-scraper"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
